ology still she wasn't sure it  was enough 2015 when I graduated and  came back to Las Vegas the Brewing  industry was just budding at that time  and I was really worried I wouldn't be  able to get a brewing job here but she  did though she admits at times it was  still a boys club at events and  conferences he was our sellerman and I  was the Brewer and everybody would talk  to him and he's like I'm not the Brewer  talk to her then she got the call from  bad beat they needed a head Brewer it  was her shot sometimes I will sit back  and think you know wow this is you know  so much easier now than it used to be  and she's passing on her knowledge  Becca Halpin also a Trailblazer was able  to come in without a science degree easy  to learn the step-by-step process open  this valve press this button you know  add this at this time but learning why  things react the way they react is just  so much more vast and takes takes years  to really figure that out but she says  she feels confident in her roles  assistant Brewer because of the culture  at bad beat they're doing it for the  community around you for other people  that can enjoy it and you can enjoy it  too and these ladies certainly do I  can't believe that this is what I do for  a living Heather Mills eight news now  so there are laws on the books that make  it more difficult for Nevada craft  Brewers Nevada must follow a three-tier  system in order to distribute meaning  product must be sold to a wholesaler  before it sold to a retailer the Nevada  craft Brewers Association is working on  changing more of those laws though in  the upcoming legislative session
 

